#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e0dc1c3-210c-5bca-a788-1a8e3ae5aa5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293206} {:answer/id #uuid "9e5db305-e741-5c95-b785-661bf4589106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293207} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec70a2e-1ad7-5fda-b8de-b5e200aa8ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293208} {:answer/id #uuid "02c1490b-2304-57b0-ae21-f557180a5938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293209} {:answer/id #uuid "11239261-2fd4-5af3-89ad-fcad1c9e9621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11239261-2fd4-5af3-89ad-fcad1c9e9621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293210} :answer-field/id #uuid "78028f31-056b-5364-8107-f135cf6c2c43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "215232ce-c44e-5876-848b-764311244f79" :question/math-academy-id "q-30872" :question/problem "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+14x-5$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-6{x}^{2}+14x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-5x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-2{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-5c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-2{c}^{2}+7c-5 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}-7c+5 & =0 \\\\ (c-1)(2c-5) & =0 \\\\ c & =1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293211 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be6a37d7-62f4-53f8-833b-534cf983c83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293213} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a898a6-66e6-5802-84f6-63fa5a1e03d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{16}-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9a898a6-66e6-5802-84f6-63fa5a1e03d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{16}-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293214} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ec9cd8e-8d1e-5d0a-964b-6930c346238a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b35a20f7-a229-5f61-92db-08090927f688" :question/math-academy-id "q-316309" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/assets/1c69b5a43e445861a728fcd8faed9e89b3bcb61141ad35d99e60f2a43983244d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-2,9],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(5,0)$ with radius $3.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[0,8].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,8].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8-0}\\cdot (-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc96793-beac-5813-aa2c-a00493884514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{61.2}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293217} {:answer/id #uuid "4086c4ab-277f-5a4b-80e4-6468e51e9be5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50.0}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293218} {:answer/id #uuid "879925b4-e44a-5ae1-ba63-3d2d0d84faf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{52.1}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293219} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cf9b1f-8736-5d0f-a4e0-9358d2c8a919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{56.5}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293220} {:answer/id #uuid "182718cb-3d0e-5062-9eca-0f720915804e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58.9}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "182718cb-3d0e-5062-9eca-0f720915804e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58.9}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293221} :answer-field/id #uuid "96027c73-d970-5a5d-8d9b-19336d1c17a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d52db9f0-626b-5e49-b54e-8b0ef2daded7" :question/math-academy-id "q-3289" :question/problem "During the winter in Pasadena, the temperature, in ${F}^{∘}$, $t$ hours after $9$ a.m. can be modeled by the function $T(t)=50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}).$ Find the average temperature during the period from $9$ a.m. to $9$ p.m." :question/worked-solution "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,12].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12-0}{\\int }_{0}^{12}(50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{12}(50t-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(50\\cdot 12-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 12}{12}))-(50\\cdot 0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{12}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\frac{600\\pi +168}{\\pi }+\\frac{168}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{600\\pi +336}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{600\\pi +336}{12\\pi } \\\\  & ≈{58.9}^{∘}F.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82af23ef-7949-544f-9cad-3f3a9c083e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099378} {:answer/id #uuid "98215740-9e83-5075-8c42-42754f1a1106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099379} {:answer/id #uuid "9a461384-2d5e-59f6-8841-b9c9c47941c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099380} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c2c956-b0fd-5933-84b4-f4e364efc652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099381} {:answer/id #uuid "e659d148-22cb-50d2-b54b-a9fbb255aa8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a461384-2d5e-59f6-8841-b9c9c47941c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099380} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd53058e-bd9f-551c-9090-3f5bf4416dfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7eacf291-9083-5337-9223-5109e18f5b01" :question/math-academy-id "q-3293" :question/problem "Find the number $c>0$ such that the average value of $f(x)=9+8x-3{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(9+8x-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(9x+4{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(9c+4{c}^{2}-{c}^{3})-(0)] \\\\ -3 & =9+4c-{c}^{2} \\\\ {c}^{2}-4c-12 & =0 \\\\ (c+2)(c-6) & =0 \\\\ c & =-2,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $c>0,$ we conclude that $c=6$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c32c5273-8ba9-50b1-a7a4-bfbaed8ca922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c32c5273-8ba9-50b1-a7a4-bfbaed8ca922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293224} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff332df-3755-50c1-b809-235e8cb7ad94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50c4bf2d-5c40-5d7e-8775-995cfa67f088" :question/math-academy-id "q-344695" :question/problem "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ on the interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3}{\\pi }(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
